{
  "delta_from_prior": "Acknowledges that Neon54/55 K6 near-parity examples were falsified (peak 0, root IALH-5 UNSAT via globally combined congruences). Replaces our prior 21-variable disjoint-pair bipartite product fixture (neon_worstcase_auto_00130, 6x3 pairs) and Neon58 (4x4 pairs) with a 20-variable, 265-clause lifted odd-cycle transversal contradiction (C_5 + C_5) x C_5 whose exact 15-variable, 80-clause quotient has zero link-twins and no bipartite pair-product structure, defeating Fable73's proposed link-twin contraction while still passing exact GF(2) compression, resisting both stages of core_refutation, and keeping IALH-5 work bounded.",
  "explanation": "### 1. Code Audit of Pinned v5 (`blq-composed-core-scc-emra-ialh5-v5`)\nAuditing the supplied exact solver, `compression.py`, `core_refutation.py`, `check_scc_and_growth.py`, `test_elim.py`, and `test_mra.py` reveals **no soundness bug** (`correctness_fixture` not found):\n- **`compression.py` (`_verify_certificate`)**: Partitions every normalized original clause into exact-support blocks (`len(counts) == len(blocks)`, `sum(counts) == len(quotient)`), rejects duplicate/tautological literals, enforces `forms[i] & ~mask == 0` so each quotient coordinate referenced in a block depends only on that block's support, checks `evaluate(clauses, x) == evaluate(q, image)` on all `points(support)`, and verifies `P * L = I_r` entrywise over GF(2) for surjectivity. Together with `run_counting` passing `variables(quotient)` to `run_counting_core`, exact equisatisfiability is preserved.\n- **`core_refutation.py` (`probe`) & composed core**: Enforces an independent subset check (`set(core).issubset(set(f))`), requires `compress_root(core)` to succeed, and only returns `UNSAT` when the compressed core quotient is 2-SAT and `two_sat(q)` is False. Applying `probe` once to the exact quotient is sound by equisatisfiability.\n- **Residual solver**: `refute` builds UP-surviving tables on windows of width <= 5 and independently checks every local congruence and the global dual with exact `Fraction` arithmetic (`verify_certificate`/`verify_dual`); `canon_plus` (UP + subsumption + signed SCC), size-nonincreasing `elim_plus`, and subsumption `prune` (`below(g, h)` implies `models(g) <= models(h)`) are all sound.\n\n### 2. Acknowledgment of Prior Receipts & Residual Mechanism\nWe acknowledge that Neon54/55 K6 near-parity examples are falsified as growth witnesses (actual peak 0, root IALH-5 UNSAT via globally combined lattice congruences) and that our prior 21-variable fixture (`neon_worstcase_auto_00130`) and `Neon58` both relied on disjoint-pair bipartite products, which expose link-twins (`(a_i, b_i)` pairs) to Fable73's proposed nonlinear link-twin contraction and pair-grouped branching orders.\n\nTo move beyond disjoint-pair products while still testing scalable local-certificate compression (not a mere skip) and avoiding timeout, we target three exact properties of v5:\n1. `compress_root` selects quotient basis forms in descending order of `(-block_count, popcount, mask)`, and `run_counting` branches on `variables(quotient)` in ascending order.\n2. `windows(k=5)` ignores width-6 clauses entirely, and any width-<=5 monotone/transversal table containing the zero vector plus all unit vectors (or all-ones plus all co-unit vectors) has integer affine hull Z^w (`hull_rows == []`).\n3. `elim_plus` is blocked when every variable has high enough negative degree relative to non-tautological positive occurrences.\n\n### 3. Fixture Construction: Lifted `(C_5 \\sqcup C_5) \\times C_5` Odd-Cycle Transversal (20 vars, 265 clauses)\nWe construct an exact 20-variable, 265-clause UNSAT formula (all clauses width 6, 80 exact-support blocks) that compresses cleanly to a 15-variable, 80-clause **twin-free, non-product** quotient `F_Q = (C_5^(1) \\sqcup C_5^(2)) \\times C_5^(R)`:\n- **Left side (unlifted variables `1..10`)**:\n  - `C_5^(1)` on `(1, 5, 3, 7, 9)` (edges `[1,5], [3,5], [3,7], [7,9], [1,9]`) with 5 minimal vertex covers (MVCs) of size 3: `{1,5,7}, {3,5,9}, {1,3,7}, {5,7,9}, {1,3,9}`.\n  - `C_5^(2)` on `(2, 6, 4, 8, 10)` (edges `[2,6], [4,6], [4,8], [8,10], [2,10]`) with 5 MVCs of size 3: `{2,6,8}, {4,6,10}, {2,4,8}, {6,8,10}, {2,4,10}`.\n  - **25 left negative width-6 clauses**: all 5 x 5 pairs `T_1 \\cup T_2` of one MVC from `C_5^(1)` and one from `C_5^(2)`. Satisfying these forces at least one edge of `C_5^(1) \\sqcup C_5^(2)` to be all-zero.\n- **Right side (lifted via 5 XOR pairs on `11..20`)**:\n  - `C_5^(R)` on quotient forms `c_1 = 11^12, c_2 = 13^14, c_3 = 15^16, c_4 = 17^18, c_5 = 19^20` (edges `(c_1,c_2), (c_2,c_3), (c_3,c_4), (c_4,c_5), (c_1,c_5)`).\n  - **40 right negative width-6 clauses**: each of the 5 MVCs of `C_5^(R)` (`{c_1,c_2,c_4}, {c_2,c_3,c_5}, {c_1,c_3,c_4}, {c_2,c_4,c_5}, {c_1,c_3,c_5}`) forbids `(1,1,1)` and lifts to 2^3 = 8 clauses by expanding each `-c_j` to `(+u_j,-v_j)` or `(-u_j,+v_j)`. Satisfying these forces at least one edge of `C_5^(R)` to be all-zero.\n- **200 cross positive width-6 clauses**: for each of the 10 left edges `e` and 5 right edges `(c_p, c_q)`, the quotient clause `(e \\lor c_p \\lor c_q)` forbids `(0,0,0,0)` and lifts to 2^2 = 4 clauses by expanding each `+c_j` to `(+u_j,+v_j)` or `(-u_j,-v_j)`.\n- **UNSAT proof**: Left negative clauses force an all-zero edge `e` in `C_5^(1) \\sqcup C_5^(2)`; right negative clauses force an all-zero edge `f` in `C_5^(R)`; the cross block for `(e, f)` is then falsified.\n\n### 4. Predicted Behavior on Pinned v5 (Compression, Core, and Residual Growth)\n- **Exact compression succeeds (not a discovery failure)**: 80 blocks of width 6 use `80 * 64 = 5120 <= 16384` local points and ~437k verification work `<< 8M`. Each unlifted left variable `1..10` appears in `15 + 10 = 25` block annihilators (weight 1), each lifted right form `c_1..c_5` appears in `3 + 20 = 23` blocks (weight 2), and every non-singleton combination appears in at most 11 blocks. Thus `compress_root` deterministically selects `[1..10, c_1..c_5]` with zero greedy incompatibility, yielding the exact 15-variable, 80-clause quotient `F_Q` with ascending order starting at the four non-adjacent vertices `1, 2, 3, 4` (`a_1, b_1, a_3, b_3`).\n- **Core refutation returns UNKNOWN at both stages**: In the original 265-clause input, every block has size 1, 4, or 8 and is already a complete affine subspace (stabilizer size = block size), so `probe` removes 0 clauses (`no_clauses_removed`). In the 80-clause quotient, every block has size 1, so `probe` again removes 0 clauses.\n- **Residual growth (`peak >= 4`, expected ~10\u201312) with controlled total work**: At the root of `F_Q`, all 25 left negative clauses have width 6 (invisible to `windows(k=5)`), all width-<=5 windows have full integer hull Z^w (0 IALH-5 constraints), and `elim_plus` is stuck (every variable has product >= 60 vs <= 25 clauses). Branching on `1, 2, 3, 4` (`a_1, b_1, a_3, b_3`) yields 2 states at layer 1, 4 at layer 2, 7 at layer 3, and ~11\u201312 pairwise incomparable states at layer 4 (`elim_plus` only simplifies the `(0,0)` branch where `a_3, b_3` drop, while `(0,1), (1,0), (1,1)` stay stuck and split). As soon as any left edge becomes all-zero at deeper layers, `C_5^(R)` reduces to 5 binary edges plus 5 MVCs on 5 variables, which `refute` closes immediately via `empty_table`, keeping total runtime well below 20s.\n\n### 5. Challenge to Fable's Link-Twin Contraction & Fibre-Transfer Proposals\nUnlike `Neon58` and `neon_worstcase_auto_00130`, `F_Q` has **zero link-twins** (every vertex has degree 2 in an odd cycle `C_5`; no two variables share a positive clause neighborhood) and **no disjoint-pair product structure**. Fable73's link-twin contraction finds zero contractible pairs on `F_Q`, and pair-grouping branch orders do not apply. Moreover, deleting any single lifted cross block (4 clauses, 1 quotient clause `(e \\lor f)`) yields a **SAT** nearby control (set `e = 0`, remaining left vertices `1`; `f = 0`, remaining right vertices `1`), demonstrating that unverified clause-dropping or approximate fibre-collapse heuristics risk false UNSAT unless paired with an exact certificate. This is a finite growth fixture, not a general asymptotic lower bound.",
